<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
QuartzFire SSL Inspection component version.

The postinst feeds this file's directory to vyos-1x's
xml_ref/generate_cache.py, which registers `quartzfire-ssl-inspection` in the
system component-version set (vyos.component_version.version_info_from_system).
That version is stamped into every saved config.boot footer, and the boot-time
migrator (the `migrate activate configure` step run by vyos-router) applies the
matching config-migrate/migrate/quartzfire-ssl-inspection/<n>-to-<n+1> scripts
to bring an older config.boot up to this version.

It MUST live in the same xml-dir as the interface definition (the postinst
passes that directory to generate_cache.py) and be valid interfaceDefinition
XML (no nodes — only the syntaxVersion tag), exactly as vyos-1x ships its own
interface-definitions/xml-component-version.xml.

Bump the version whenever the `service quartzfire ssl-inspection` CLI grammar
changes incompatibly, and ship a matching <old>-to-<new> migration script.

History:
  1  interface-scoped model (`... ssl-inspection interface <ethX>`) replaced by
     per-firewall-rule policies (`... ssl-inspection policy <rule-number>`);
     see migration-scripts/quartzfire-ssl-inspection/0-to-1.
-->
<interfaceDefinition>
  <syntaxVersion component="quartzfire-ssl-inspection" version="1"/>
</interfaceDefinition>
